  SECOM.HL
		D.C.T. 2-DEC-80
   This is a description of what the various .ft programs labeled 
secom?.ft do.
    SECOM1.FT  is the sequence comparison program that searches the 
atlas using only one peptide. This prog chains to SCOM1B.SV
    SECOM2.FT is the same as secom1 but uses multiple runs.  It needs 
subroutine SSW(N) and chains to SCOM1A.SV
    SECOM3.FT is subroutine SECM3.  It computes a omparison matrix, the
Sankoff V0 matrix and does a diagonal search.
    SECOM4.FT tests for possible internal sequence homology.
    SECOM5.FT can be used for the comparison of 2 proteins up to 1000
residues in length. Diagonal search on only 2 proteins.
    SECOM.FT is the Sankoff procedure.  up to 10 proteins per family.
    SECOMX.FT is the same as SECOM.FT but the scores are multiplied by
10.  is only works for zero centered matrices.  The programs in this 
set are: SECL, SANKOF, TRACEB.
    	SECL.FT,SANKOF.FT,TRACEB.FT (all as .SV files on SYS:) are used 
in connection with secom and secomx for the Sankoff procedure.
		8-OCT-82  DESCRIPTIONS:
     SECOM4.F4 (and .LD file) and SECOM5.F4 (and .LD) are fortran IV
versions of SECOM4.FT and SECOM5.FT.  These programs are diagonal search
es which also keep track of the mean of the distribution.  They are
also on the VAX in SECOM5R.FOR and SECOM4R.FOR (with appropriate
command files) which also do randomizations.  I found there was an error
in SECOM4.FT and so I rewrote these programs.  The error is not large,
however.
     On the VAX there are SECOM5F.FOR,SECOM5FR.FOR, and SECOM5R.FOR.
The "F" stands for family comparison.  These family comparisons by
diagonal methods are very slow.
     The command file SECOM.COM runs the Sankoff procedure.  Command 
file SECOMR.COM runs the Sankoff randomization procedure.
     The scoring schemes are (VAX):
	DAYHFN.DA(T)   new Dayhoff scores
	MCLACH.DA(T)   McLachlan scores
	MBDSCR.DA(T)   4 - MBD
	IDENTY.DA(T)   Identity table (asx,glx are 0 vs anp &asn resp.)
		       This tabler is simply a diagonal of 1 and should 
		       be fixed up for further use.
	MBDTAB.DA(T)   This is mbd table of no use as scores
